# Update Current-State Docs After Module or TRD Changes

When you **add, change, or remove** either (1) **implementation** in a module that has a TRD in docs, or (2) **any TRD** under `docs/trd/` or its subfolders, you **must** update the corresponding **current-state** document in the same work (or explicitly leave a follow-up to do it).

**Convention:** For any TRD at `docs/trd/<path>/<name>.md` (with `<path>` possibly empty, e.g. `docs/trd/architecture/tools.md` or `docs/trd/testing_strategy.md`), the current-state doc (when it exists) is `docs/current_state/<path>/<name>.md`. If you create a new current-state doc for a TRD, add a row to the mapping below.

## Module / TRD → current-state doc mapping

| Implementation path | TRD | Current-state doc |
